# =============================================================================
# Variable catalog. This file documents EVERY variable the system reads.
# The live env files carry only `KEY=value` plus category headers — the
# explanations live here.
#
# Layering (each file overrides the previous):
#   .env         committed, non-secret base defaults (Compose-network values)
#   .env.dev     committed, ONLY the values that differ for local development
#   .env.local   gitignored, SECRETS ONLY — never anything else, never committed
#
#   .env.prod    committed, standalone production set for pasting into a host
#                panel (Dokploy/Render/Fly). Not layered with the above.
#
# The API loads these with Node's native `--env-file-if-exists` flag; no dotenv
# dependency. See apps/api/package.json.
# =============================================================================

# --- Runtime ---------------------------------------------------------------
# NODE_ENV          Secret: no.  Default: production
#                   `development` enables pretty-printed logs and relaxes the
#                   config schema. Anything else is treated as production.
# API_HOST          Secret: no.  Default: 0.0.0.0
#                   Bind address. Must stay 0.0.0.0 inside a container,
#                   otherwise the port publish cannot reach the process.
# API_PORT          Secret: no.  Default: 3000
# LOG_LEVEL         Secret: no.  Default: info
#                   Pino level: trace|debug|info|warn|error|fatal.

# --- Database --------------------------------------------------------------
# POSTGRES_DB       Secret: no.  Default: derq
#                   Read by the `postgres` Compose service to create the DB.
# POSTGRES_USER     Secret: no.  Default: derq
#                   Read by the `postgres` Compose service to create the role.
# POSTGRES_PORT     Secret: no.  Default: 5432
#                   HOST port the `postgres` Compose service publishes on
#                   127.0.0.1. Compose-only — the API never reads it. Change it
#                   if you already run Postgres on 5432, and update
#                   DATABASE_URL in .env.dev to match.
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD Secret: YES. Belongs in .env.local (or the host's secret
#                   store). Compose falls back to the throwaway local value
#                   `derq_local_dev` so `docker compose up` works on a fresh
#                   clone. Never reuse that value outside your machine.
# DATABASE_URL      Secret: YES when it embeds a real password.
#                   Full libpq connection string. The API reads only this — it
#                   never assembles a DSN from parts.
#                   Example: postgres://derq:pw@postgres:5432/derq
# PG_POOL_MAX       Secret: no.  Default: 10
#                   node-postgres pool size PER API INSTANCE. The ceiling is
#                   Postgres `max_connections`; keep
#                   (PG_POOL_MAX x replicas) well under it, or put PgBouncer
#                   in front. See docs/scalability.md.
# PG_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT_MS
#                   Secret: no.  Default: 5000
#                   Server-side statement timeout. A single pathological query
#                   cannot pin a pool connection forever.

# --- HTTP ------------------------------------------------------------------
# CORS_ORIGIN       Secret: no.  Default: http://localhost:8080
#                   Comma-separated list of allowed browser origins.
# RATE_LIMIT_MAX    Secret: no.  Default: 300
#                   Requests per window, per client IP.
# RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW Secret: no.  Default: 1 minute
#                   Human-readable window accepted by @fastify/rate-limit.
# AGGREGATE_CACHE_MAX_AGE
#                   Secret: no.  Default: 60
#                   Seconds sent as `Cache-Control: public, max-age=N` on the
#                   read-only aggregate endpoints. 0 disables caching, which is
#                   what .env.dev does so edits show up immediately.

# --- Seeding ---------------------------------------------------------------
# SEED_DAYS         Secret: no.  Default: 90
#                   Days of hourly history the seed generates, ending at the
#                   current hour. Row count is derived, not configured:
#                   16 countries x 6 vehicle types x 24 h x SEED_DAYS.
#                   The default yields ~207k rows — large enough that index
#                   choice and GROUP BY plans actually matter.

# --- Frontend (apps/web, Vite) ---------------------------------------------
# NOTE: Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the PUBLIC bundle. None of them
# may ever hold a secret, so apps/web has no .env.local. Vite keys its mode
# files on build mode, so the files are .env.development / .env.production.
#
# VITE_API_URL      Secret: no.  Default: /api (same-origin, proxied by nginx)
#                   Base URL of the API. Set to http://localhost:3000/api when
#                   running the Vite dev server against a host-run API.
